  "peak_h": 0.25,
  "statement": "the anisotropy is (2/3) f_E h(g/a0) P2 and h peaks at g = a0 with h = 1/4; at 1 AU it is 1.35e-08 f_E and at Mercury 2.02e-09 f_E. Fixed-axis anisotropies of the Solar-System potential are bounded at roughly the 1e-9 level (published PPN preferred-location and solar-J2 constraints, quoted as an order of magnitude, not evaluated here), so f_E of order unity is marginal at Mercury and f_E <~ 0.3 is safe; a steeper Newtonian cutoff of h would remove the tension at the cost of one constant."
 },
